    "content" : "Here&#39;s a lengthy post about a project I&#39;ve been working on throughout the summer. It&#39;s a project that switches a valve to water plants in the garden. It has a manual switch to control the valve or an Atmel Atmega328 AVR set up as an Arduino that is used as a timer attached to a relay to display information via a 16x2 character LCD and automatically turn the valve off after a adjustable amount of time. I&#39;m really happy how it turned out and has to be one of my favorite projects so far. If you get a chance to look at it, please write a comment on what you think.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "Here's a lengthy post about a project I've been working on throughout the summer. It's a project that switches a valve to water plants in the garden. It has a manual switch to control the valve or an Atmel Atmega328 AVR set up as an Arduino that is used as a timer attached to a relay to display information via a 16x2 character LCD and automatically turn the valve off after a adjustable amount of time. I'm really happy how it turned out and has to be one of my favorite projects so far. If you get a chance to look at it, please write a comment on what you think.",
